---
import Marketing from '../layouts/Marketing.astro';
---
<Marketing
  title="Sub-processors"
  description="The third parties Total Recall uses to run the service, what each one does, and the services customers contract directly."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:760px">
      <p class="eyebrow">Sub-processors</p>
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(32px,4.6vw,52px);margin:10px 0 0">Who touches what.</h1>
      <p class="lead" style="margin:18px 0 0">
        A sub-processor is a third party we use to run the service and that may handle customer
        data on our behalf. Because your brain runs in accounts you own, our list is short, and
        most of the companies involved work for you, not for us.
      </p>

      <div style="margin-top:40px;display:grid;gap:28px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.65">
        <p style="color:var(--muted,#666);margin:0">Last updated: July 12, 2026</p>

        <div>
          <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">Our sub-processors</h2>
          <p style="margin:0 0 12px">These handle the limited data Total Recall itself holds:</p>
          <ul style="margin:0;padding-left:20px">
            <li style="margin-bottom:8px"><strong>Clerk</strong> (United States): sign-in and account identity for the theo app.</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom:8px"><strong>Vercel</strong> (United States): hosts the theo app and this website, including setup progress records and operational logs.</li>
            <li><strong>Google Workspace</strong> (United States): our company email, which holds support conversations you send us.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">Services you contract directly</h2>
          <p style="margin:0">
            The following are not our sub-processors: they are providers you sign up with
            yourself, under your own accounts and their own terms, and your brain's content
            lives with them under your control. Supabase (your database), Railway (your
            always-on services), OpenAI and Anthropic (AI processing on your own API keys), and
            the sources you choose to connect, such as Slack, Google, Notion, and Telegram. You
            can revoke or delete any of them without our involvement.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">Changes</h2>
          <p style="margin:0">
            If we add or replace a sub-processor, we will update this page and its date. The
            <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> describes what data we hold; questions to
            <a href="mailto:support@totalrecallhq.com">support@totalrecallhq.com</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Marketing>
